<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India news: Opposition protest clouds Modi's 25-year milestone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:899ca13f4e590174cdcb95333d84173773046488c0c1d3df0acf883ccfaf9ae1</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-protest-clouds-modi-s-25-year-milestone/live-79570653--dd5c6b9365a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-protest-clouds-modi-s-25-year-milestone/live-79570653?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi police has beefed up security around the Election Commission of India, likely preparing for another day of 'vote theft' protests. Meanwhile, PM Modi marks 25 years in public service. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47c288d4f0ccaea0d360d72ea51c961f2396db7f3dba3fffca21fdca8d820d9a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Mali: Junta forces retake strategic town of Kidal from separatists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:168266f6103cf8a0b3dda68af6416334d985cd9e473157564a3716073e4eaab5</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617--dc7ca7f76853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mali-junta-forces-retake-strategic-town-of-kidal-from-separatists/a-79570617?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mali's military regained control of the strategic town of Kidal after forcing Tuareg separatists and al Queda-linked jihadists to withdraw following an offensive backed by Russia's Africa Corps.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Lionel Messi plays final game for Argentina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0f8555fd6f7e763a002f354f6d40cdf571acf3c9adf883ccaa2e4407f687e56</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:12:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-lionel-messi-plays-final-game-for-argentina/a-79570608--6687ff69f964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-lionel-messi-plays-final-game-for-argentina/a-79570608?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentinian superstar Lionel Messi bowed out of international football with one last goal for his country. For football in Argentina, and indeed across the world, it's the end of an era.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Christa Pike awake after failed Tennessee execution: lawyers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f370b8d9d406b66680b770a6abdfa408b3a8a8e50e4060b6e1242d4fb7da32b</id><updated>2026-1