/><summary type="html">The company's new model, named "Le Chonk," is its first release in five months. Mistral says it outruns some of its Chinese competitors in several areas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Naked Trump statue goes on display in Strasbourg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caaf4c405a401cfda7f5854b8e781cbce9061c8ab66b77f896b17ceb979c57eb</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/naked-trump-statue-goes-on-display-in-strasbourg/a-79568640--b613f03d8e20.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/naked-trump-statue-goes-on-display-in-strasbourg/a-79568640?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Titled "The Orange Plague," a gold-coated statue presents Donald Trump sitting on a smaller man's back. The Danish artist blamed Trump for getting in the way of efforts to address climate change.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b47556392401828cafe4081fa5ca7ff9939dffb7272ccb0cb6e69830d8aed064</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d842d76e1682fcb73c7699828a671b533b13dbf710804d8c9567ce0b711abf10</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia denies anti-plague measures after pneumonia death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e888ac0b5a64de588a3633d05aaad7387454f5607093fef8a4c8ba5bc45f7a2</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T17:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-denies-anti-plague-measures-after-pneumonia-death/a-79567922--5a84d749e787.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-denies-anti-plague-measures-after-pneumonia-death/a-79567922?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of an employee at an anti-plague institute in Irkutsk is still being looked into, the authorities said. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio called for Russia to be transparent about its findings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c807e11cb616baf871f343ee466e8a6bb08a002d743abae3d9bec4488757363c</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Seventh arrest made after air base plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fd0dd987a8eee6b18bb7cadf5879b0290d639e5cad303cbe19e428a06cebc04</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-seventh-arrest-made-after-air-base-plot/a-79566985--8d48e9554e6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-seventh-arrest-made-after-air-base-plot/a-79566985?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man, a British national in his twenties, was arrested in London in suspicion of "preparing terrorist acts."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c37d5cd1a5bac594fe441b11a50a5c9383782e70f1ac92462ecd201eef35004b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain court lifts Puigdemont arrest warrant, clearing way for his return home ahead of November elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a225ab06fd9bdddeaea036b6325e4fe57faf5d0b663124f2dd0df00b6a6a1453</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-court-lifts-puigdemont-arrest-warrant-clearing-way-for-his-return-home-ahead-of-november-elect/a-79565853--7635b4e28c09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-court-lifts-puigdemont-arrest-warrant-clearing-way-for-his-return-home-ahead-of-november-elections/a-79565853?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Catalan separatist leader Carles Puigdemont fled Spain in 2017 after launching an independence bid. The court's decision means he can return home without fear of arrest after almost a decade in exile.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Southeast Asia's haze crisis: Have lessons been learned?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:545c93fce03a3b8f2e046b0cfa42f221de66870482d61226db9d83ff229398f1</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992--f0834d091bdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven years after catastrophic fires prompted promises of tougher action, Southeast Asia is again choking on transboundary haze, raising questions about whether the region has learned the lessons of 2015.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>As more Iranian women reject hijab rules, regime looks at new ways to force compliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:691eb218fde266459654e5f79d73d4d69aa20b83c2fe60c419abd1995733ef1a</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962--9c09f80416a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As more women in Iran reject rules on wearing hijab headscarves, hardliners are shifting focus from "morality police" street enforcement towards social pressure in workplaces, services and businesses.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray war may spill over to Eritrea — helped by Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's rhetoric</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:501c3a403693c737de31b4137e6798d7e8c7431f6b09096aa9e228e131d763a6</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957--f357fb8ada5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed is consolidating power, but he must contend with a regional alliance opposing him and a Tigray conflict that could spill over into Eritrea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD makes history again in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a28b0200bb102bed8398022b7fb55ca1047ddbc2cf9ab3cb5a68099a457dc72</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146--3b11bbf1dc05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the end of World War II, a German state parliament has chosen parliamentary speaker from the far right: Tobias Rausch of the Alternative for Germany (AfD).</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Literature Prize: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f99ce1f0b02de4aaa52675a689fbd1f6cb388abb8155116f80db894fdd61890e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--42983d639d88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in Literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading claims spark plague fears in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2be955fb63cd4bb843a06ffec6902f4c3f40a32ac9ea799332d21c86bb7d621</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752--eaca60a52c9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of a lab worker at a plague research institute in Russia has sparked claims about a lab accident, hundreds of infections and international spread. Some of these viral narratives are misleading.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>AI models keep hacking real systems during tests. What does this mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9da90a1a220ffba847fce7aba8967343af57a61000e091e632533b9ee1c1edc1</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943--07f5722af213.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI models have repeatedly broken into real commercial and government systems during safety tests during 2026. Cybersecurity researcher Thorsten Holz explains what that means, and why he isn't expecting a robot uprising.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces a triple threat from Russia, China and domestic far-right extremists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94570b51bf3c7de64080565e57987ba636f990bc3ba0f81cd162d6b8c3681aa6</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-a-triple-threat-from-russia-china-and-domestic-far-right-extremists/a-79560490--8059184d93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-a-triple-threat-from-russia-china-and-domestic-far-right-extremists/a-79560490?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a rare public hearing Germany's intelligence agencies identified Russia as the country's most dangerous adversary. The threat from China is also coming into focus. And the homegrown far right also poses a challenge.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Far-right AfD gets first house speaker in a German state parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0eb194b9a7f700352e412092c9f520651b929feb808f633fbd22bc6144e4140</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497--5fb1cf58f705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since World War II, a far-right party has a house speaker in a German state parliament. And Germany's foreign minister has warned that the climate crisis could fuel extremism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ee16ff86d9ece07d6c291b50a6d6be6161092ad9ee03b7175607644f6d69aa3</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australia, New Zealand probe Flydubai pilot's time there</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8739eef1fb8a92128e64f2fd9cba3a66da00a6bf907f815956f4a51d294d3a38</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-new-zealand-probe-flydubai-pilot-s-time-there/a-79551423--4e0d79ffea0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-new-zealand-probe-flydubai-pilot-s-time-there/a-79551423?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Flydubai pilot from Oman suspected of trying to crash a plane in Israel spent time in Oceania as a young man. Police in both Australia and New Zealand said they would investigate his links to the countries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: Has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd601e06d1491c77b6c57034e086864eee3fa432b203b4f4e4d2365f095e1520</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trust in the German Constitutional Court is eroding — how can this be stopped?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e36e965fd498a94d73793d8b34d844887dc6cbbcd10ac8eb0007057e8ae440c6</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211--cc048545c82f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's top court, which turned 75 this year, is losing the population's trust, surveys show. Some say reforms in the way it picks candidates would help, to also accept candidates nominated by the far-right AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Spy chief warns Russia conflict risk growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73373ea8d31482734e6772daa6136528c5ab1b013844047e97f38d88810b78be</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789--3bde17a9e96c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is already waging a "shadow war" against Europe, the head of Germany's foreign intelligence service says. The Left Party is taking a case over remarks by the CDU's Katherina Reiche to a top court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20169ef4795d464d9601c45890d76b18bfbae8434e1ce50a62b886a131ac60ba</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A worker at a plague research institute in Siberia has died, and nearly 200 of her contacts are under medical observation. Russian authorities deny a link to the bacterial infection. The US is monitoring the situation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp faces myriad of issues after rough start with Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4a1d950e70153cbcd82376860cdff8a59e02a822e15eeee647c0ce3d38