-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:215149488582d30ce9a491d8c48b614c46c5dd61ee2d901b1c71ff5c86b7cb4e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97904dfaa4bf8b1e1a38d5b60a8d487215936176644386adeae7cfa0c28b494b</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen ends collective wage agreements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eab2725eca841d9dab87a765b4276a814196757f8980ba858ac1b29c01d0e60d</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802--2228595954e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an effort to cut costs, automaker Volkswagen terminated most of its collective wage agreements in Germany. This could reignite disputes with employee representatives.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino is a 'postcard from the future' — and could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4560c5665c22c6ceee76c1033a06c689b295038438190401876976b21d2a3adb</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945--e1a2336874a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current El Nino could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths. Researchers warn it offers a glimpse of temperatures that may become normal within 20 years.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9494ae088f8fb7e554febd4108890f2d934dbf15aa543998731f8116e767d6f</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714--fef6c98dbd47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Park satirist pushes for accountability in Cornell gang-rape lawsuit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27ab0938deb5ab5057c53a82e19d21ae5acc3d4829d9da4149eb1a095719da93</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382--e2bb4e991ce2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Writer Toby Morton is using a new website to amplify allegations in a high-profile sexual assault lawsuit involving seven Cornell students. The reopening of the case is causing an outcry on social media.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham seeks 'hope again' at Labour Party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa1e8762c2098168fbd9beff19a25d8c1399aa2ea5ab667557b75a501256794d</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376--71e603fc9e60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham is seeking a delicate balance between optimism and realism at Labour's annual party conference. He promised hope and an end to "politics as usual" but also an "honest conversation" about difficult dilemmas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: As corruption cases multiply, experts question whether the anti-corruption drive is addressing the causes or just the symptoms.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bced569a13d01cc95491550a4eeffff354243ef8b9dd516c33e94fdcbda3792e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressin/a-79473031--8c7e71b0b3b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressing-the-causes-or-just-the-symptoms/a-79473031?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a former president to the ex-intelligence chief, Albania is prosecuting senior officials at a rate once thought impossible. But do more prosecutions mean less corruption or simply better enforcement?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6787f87035fd567baf07d101deb587be8edadd8772eeb003295dc6b51dd91ec2</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:1